WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:04.590
Marvel movies are great, but their characters
are usually just a screen-friendly shadow

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:05.919
of their ink-and-paper origins.

00:00:05.919 --> 00:00:11.330
While some are spot on, the Avengers' movies
costumes don't always do the originals justice.

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:14.070
Here's how the Avengers should really look…

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.240
Hawkeye and Black Widow

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.849
For the big screen, Clint Barton dropped his
pointy mask and traditional uniform for a

00:00:19.849 --> 00:00:21.010
tactical look.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:25.570
But in 2012, Hawkeye's comic costume was redesigned
to look more like the film's version.

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:28.189
And less like a scaly, purple Wolverine.

00:00:28.189 --> 00:00:31.980
Both versions of Hawkeye are master marksmen
and former agents of SHIELD.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:37.180
But movie Hawkeye has a secret civilian family,
while comics Hawkeye gets around with romantic

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:39.960
relationships with Black Widow and Mockingbird,
a.k.a. Bobbi Morse.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:40.960
Fun fact!

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:44.980
Mockingbird later appeared on Agents of SHIELD,
but in a completely different relationship.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:48.800
On the other hand, after Black Widow’s comics
outfit underwent a significant change in Amazing

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.220
Spider-Man #86, she’s barely changed her
modern look.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:57.190
Both comic book and MCU versions share the
basics: red hair, black bodysuit, and wrist-mounted

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.190
weapons.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.190
They're nearly identical in the ways that
matter.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:03.620
Despite appearing in five different movies,
we still don't know much about movie Black

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:04.920
Widow.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.380
Age of Ultron's flashbacks revealed a little
of her history—specifically her training

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:10.780
to be a Soviet assassin from a young age.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:14.899
She switched sides after Hawkeye spared her
life and has been a good guy ever since.

00:01:14.899 --> 00:01:19.180
Her comic counterpart has the same broad strokes,
including her Soviet training and defection

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:20.479
to America.

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:24.439
Pretty sure that Natasha's never been Tony
Stark's assistant in the comics though.

00:01:24.439 --> 00:01:25.820
Captain America And Falcon

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:31.990
MCU Captain America is undeniably classic
Cap, but his costume often changes subtly.

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:35.770
Like his shield: originally, it was simply,
well, shield-shaped.

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:38.140
Soon it evolved into the frisbee he flings
today.

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:42.740
In all the ways that count, the MCU's Captain
America is almost completely comic-faithful.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:47.100
In the movies, Cap's a patriotic mascot before
he becomes a hero, even using a shield similar

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.039
to his early comic appearances.

00:01:49.039 --> 00:01:53.310
In the comics, Cap goes undercover as a bumbling
private who's sent on secret missions.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:58.020
Since then, comic book Cap has lost his powers,
regained them, died, un-died, and even thought

00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:59.380
he was a HYDRA agent.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:01.649
So movie Cap's got plenty to look forward
to.

00:02:01.649 --> 00:02:05.520
In the comics, Cap's longtime partner, the
Falcon, wears funky super-suit with enormous

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:10.369
red wings and a plunging neckline, resulting
in plenty of unprotected, bare chest.

00:02:10.369 --> 00:02:14.030
Movie Falcon is a somewhat more realistic
ex-paratrooper in army clothes and a set of

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:16.370
highly-advanced, technological wings.

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:21.130
Not a military man, comics Falcon is an ex-criminal
who was...mentally fused with a falcon by

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:22.130
the Red Skull.

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:25.380
Like Aquaman, but on land, Falcon has limited
control over all birds.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:29.500
If you ever see Falcon hanging around a pack
of ostriches, just run.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:33.370
Interestingly, it remains to be seen if we'll
ever see Sam Wilson wield the shield...like

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:36.349
he did in the comics in 2014.

00:02:36.349 --> 00:02:37.349
Thor

00:02:37.349 --> 00:02:41.901
Thor's first appearance in 1962 featured the
largest helmet wings you've ever seen, and

00:02:41.901 --> 00:02:43.970
kneepads that'd make a goalie blush.

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:47.159
Movie Thor occasionally wears the helmet,
and makes the practical choice to cover his

00:02:47.159 --> 00:02:48.319
arms in armor.

00:02:48.319 --> 00:02:49.410
And that beard?

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:51.790
Comics' Odinson generally prefers a clean
shave.

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:55.750
Interestingly, the movies largely ignore Thor's
onetime alter-ego, Donald Blake.

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:59.400
Originally, Thor suffered amnesia and was
trapped in the body of a disabled doctor for

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.130
years before accidentally rediscovering his
hammer.

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:07.210
He also fell for nurse Jane Foster, who's
obviously a far cry from the MCU's storm-chasing

00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:08.210
Jane.

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:11.210
In fact, pick up a recent comic book and you'll
be surprised to discover that Jane Foster

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:12.700
is Thor.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.159
Jane Fos-Thor.

00:03:14.159 --> 00:03:15.390
Heh.

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:17.349
Comics are complicated.

00:03:17.349 --> 00:03:19.409
Scarlet Witch And Quicksilver

00:03:19.409 --> 00:03:23.000
The MCU created a less revealing costume for
its Scarlet Witch.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.670
In the comics, she wears a skimpy bodysuit
and a weird headdress.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:31.299
Fortunately for Marvel’s MPAA rating, her
on-screen costume is more "autumn fashion

00:03:31.299 --> 00:03:33.770
collection" than "naughty magician's assistant."

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:34.770
Also kind of different?

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:35.909
Her powers.

00:03:35.909 --> 00:03:40.079
In the comics, she wields "chaos magic," while
in the movies her abilities are a lot less

00:03:40.079 --> 00:03:41.319
defined.

00:03:41.319 --> 00:03:44.230
She basically, and pretty inconsistently,
changes probability.

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:45.730
Good for Vegas.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:48.510
Not always great at fighting an army of Ultrons.

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:51.470
Still better than the ‘90s Iron Man Animated
Series Scarlet Witch, though.

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:55.390
"La la la la la, la la la la la"

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:58.620
Yeesh.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:02.960
Comics Quicksilver has worn a lot of costumes,
ranging from a green with a lightning bolt,

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.799
all the way to blue with…a lightning bolt.

00:04:05.799 --> 00:04:09.390
The movies cleverly and subtly incorporated
the pattern, so this is another instance where

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:11.120
we're glad they ditched the spandex.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:14.840
Sure, Quicksilver is really, really fast;
that's hard to screw up.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:18.650
He also started out his career as a villain
before joining the Avengers, not unlike the

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:22.810
MCU's version...though comics Quicksilver
doesn't die on his first adventure.

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:25.770
Instead, he marries an Inhuman woman and has
a full life.

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:31.740
Let's not even touch Ultimate Quicksilver...and
his romantic relationship with his sister.

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:34.800
Let's leave that for Star Wars, shall we?

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.150
Uueehh

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:37.160
Vision

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:41.900
On the page, Vision's an android with a simple
design: bright red face, green and yellow

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:42.900
costume.

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:45.050
It's punctuated with a solar jewel on his
forehead.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:49.300
Movie Vision is distinctly more robot-like,
covered with mechanical patterns, as though

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:52.360
the designers wanted folks to be sure that
this guy's a robot.

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:54.120
The giant yellow comics collar?

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:55.120
Gone.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:58.390
The biggest difference is that while Vision's
solar jewel is powerful in the comics, it's

00:04:58.390 --> 00:05:01.520
nothing like the Infinity Stone his live-action
counterpart wears.

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:05.880
On the other hand, Vision and Scarlet Witch
are an item in both the comics and the movies.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:07.699
Ah, romance.

00:05:07.699 --> 00:05:08.710
Hulk

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:13.250
Movie Hulk and comics Hulk are both big green
rage monsters, but MCU Hulk leapfrogged over

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:14.700
his original look.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.860
When Bruce Banner first transformed, he was
gray.

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:22.289
Hulk soon turned green, but occasionally turned
gray again, switching wildly between smart

00:05:22.289 --> 00:05:26.199
and stupid depending on the color and whatever
the writers wanted to to do at the time.

00:05:26.199 --> 00:05:30.250
Comics Hulk became irradiated during a heroic
act, but movie Hulk turns into a monster because

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:31.650
of a failed science experiment.

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:36.509
It took years for comics Hulk to change from
a semi-intelligent grey dude into an incoherent

00:05:36.509 --> 00:05:40.690
green dude, but Hulk's film transformation
omitted Hulk's sad decline into madness.

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:42.740
He just started out stupid.

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:43.880
And that Black Widow romance?

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:45.920
Ya know, the one that came outa nowhere?

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:47.979
Straight-up movie bunk.

00:05:47.979 --> 00:05:49.460
Black Panther

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:53.500
Prince T'Challa hasn't changed much, usually
just some variation on black spandex.

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:57.840
Occasionally, he makes a mouth-hole, and sometimes
he rocks a cape, necklace of teeth, or gold

00:05:57.840 --> 00:05:59.030
accoutrements.

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:01.370
Movie Panther is much of the same so far.

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:05.140
In the comics, Wakanda wasn't known to the
U.S. until it traps the Fantastic Four.

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:09.220
But by the time we meet movie Black Panther,
his country's already set up diplomatic relations

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:10.980
with the rest of the world.

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:14.400
Sadly, we'll never see Black Panther's marriage
to the X-Men's Storm, because those movie

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:16.710
universes just can't touch.

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:17.970
Ant-Man

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:21.819
During Ant-Man's early comic appearances,
he had the spandex-and-underwear look, and

00:06:21.819 --> 00:06:23.650
his helmet was a huge silver dome.

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:26.120
Solid sci-fi, but bad on the big screen.

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:29.419
Fortunately, the movie hero's outfit looks
much more like a high-powered fight suit.

00:06:29.419 --> 00:06:33.180
While both helmets have an ant-like appearance,
the MCU version nails it.

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:36.920
There's more than one Ant-Man in both the
MCU and the comics.

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:40.800
Comics Hank Pym hung with the original Avengers,
and Scott Lang later stole the suit from Pym

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.539
to help his family, which should sound familiar.

00:06:43.539 --> 00:06:48.090
The movies mix and match timelines, Ant-Men,
and evil corporations…but it's hard to argue

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.039
with the awesome results.

00:06:50.039 --> 00:06:51.259
Spider-Man

00:06:51.259 --> 00:06:56.430
Since debuting in Civil War, Spidey's accurate
super-suit made fans crazy happy.

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:59.510
No raised webbing, no energy drink logos—just
pure Spider-Man.

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:02.250
Still, MCU Spidey has some weird half-belt.

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.099
What's that about?

00:07:04.099 --> 00:07:07.880
Like most other comic heroes, Spidey has worn
roughly a million different costumes since

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:11.970
his first appearance, but his current MCU
costume is a totally fair average of the classic

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:13.350
red and blues.

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:15.409
War Machine And Iron Man

00:07:15.409 --> 00:07:20.120
Also known as 'gray Iron Man,' War Machine's
always been a variation on Tony's armor.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:24.229
Movie War Machine is extremely comic accurate—but
the Iron Patriot's a different story.

00:07:24.229 --> 00:07:27.710
In Iron Man 3, Rhodey's armor gets a patriotic
paint job.

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:32.470
But in the comics, the Iron Patriot is actually
Norman Osborn, better known as the Green Goblin.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:36.169
Osborn is, of course, completely insane, and
the armor provided an extra layer of protection

00:07:36.169 --> 00:07:37.770
from public scrutiny.

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:41.169
Because how could anyone waving an American
flag possibly be evil?

00:07:41.169 --> 00:07:43.199
Movie Iron Man is damn near perfect.

00:07:43.199 --> 00:07:46.770
Even though Tony's changed armors more times
than most people change their underwear, his

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:48.220
films' armors are really comic-accurate.

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:49.940
And under the armor?

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:51.990
Robert Downey Jr. was born for the role.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:55.789
Still, the cocky billionaire from the movies
is a caveman compared to comic book Tony,

00:07:55.789 --> 00:08:00.150
who was recently flying around in his Bleeding
Edge armor, which is conveniently stored inside

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:01.550
his body.

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:02.550
Not gross at all.

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:05.599
Kinda makes that armor suitcase in Iron Man
2 look like a pile of fancy trash.

00:08:05.599 --> 00:08:06.960
Thanks for watching!

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:09.690
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:11.990
And leave us a comment to let us know which
is your favorite Marvel costume…

